mbles (\"By mess of this spell...\") - the effect ladder and the -1/-2/-3 save adjustments still pin. - the fabricate block pins clean. - the sending block pins clean except the family casting-time cell.  rules/ua/uamuspells6.h (the The UA NEW MAGIC-USER SPELLS (pp. 66-71) pins, R360: the): 6th-level spell descriptions - chain lightning, contingency, ensnarement, eyebite, the Mordenkainen lucubration and transmute water to dust.  Pin-era pattern (R322): pinned data only - no engine site exists.  JUDGMENTs (the decode method): - the digit-garble family (the R343 precedent): the casting-time and duration 7s decode as 1 - the contingency \"7 day/level\" as 1 day/level, the eyebite and lucubration \"7 segment\" as 1 segment. The range 7s stay as printed (the ensnarement \"7\"\" below): the family decodes a range cell only when corroborated (the flaming sphere prose, the R352 cloudburst seam, the druid water-to-dust seam below) - pending the PDF. The water-to-dust \"7 cubic\" area decodes as 1 - corroborated by the druid seam in rules/ua/uadruidspells6.h. - the R342 MU table seam loses the whole 6th-level column - no 6th-level seam fn exists; every 6th-level name pins from the section bodies and the gap item list. - the ensnarement name header is lost - the section opens with a bare open-paren-C fragment; the name pins from the gap item list and the prose (the \"ensnarement spell\" self-references). The stat block prints clean after the scrambled head. - the eyebite header garbles the school tail (\"harm, lllusion/F tasm\") - the school is a hole pending the PDF, not pinned as data. The components cell prints \"V\" plus a garbled sign - flagged pending the PDF. A scrambled note has the creatures saving at +4 - flagged pending the PDF. - the lucubration name header is lost - the section opens with a bare \"sl\" fragment; the name pins from the gap item list and the prose (the \"Mordenkainen Lucubration\" self-reference). The duration cell is lost - the \"Instantaneous\" line prints as a bare stat fragment. - the water-to-dust header prints the short name only; the full name \"Transmute Water To Dust\" pins from the R342 spell-table seam and the druid spell of the same name. The magic-user print gives a 6-segment casting against the druid seam 8 - flagged as a print discrepancy (the cloudburst precedent), pinned as printed. - the chain lightning range cell truncates after the base 4 - the per-level tail is a hole pending the PDF, the base pins as printed. The saving throw cell garbles a \"2 fraction (\"2 or Neg.\") - the save pins from the prose (a half-damage save per strike plus a hit-arc save), the cell flagged pending the PDF.",
